window.docContents[51].resolve({"/Huber-rings-and-Tate-rings/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Huber-rings-and-Tate-rings":{"contents":"A topological ring  is a Huber ring (or -adic ring) if it admits a\npair of definition: an open subring  together with a finitely\ngenerated ideal  such that the subspace topology on \nequals the -adic topology — equivalently, the powers  form a\nneighbourhood basis of  in . In Adic-Spaces the pair is the structure\n and the predicate is the class\n. Following Wedhorn §6.\n\nA Tate ring is a Huber ring () that contains a\ntopologically nilpotent unit  with  — a\npseudo-uniformiser, the role of a uniformising parameter in non-archimedean\ngeometry. In Adic-Spaces this is the class . Following\nWedhorn Definition 6.10.\n\n","context":"Adic Spaces — Lean blueprint","header":"1. Huber rings and Tate rings","id":"/Huber-rings-and-Tate-rings/#Adic-Spaces-___-Lean-blueprint--Huber-rings-and-Tate-rings"}});